Waypoint
Third-party data

Airlines: waypoint/storage/airlines.tsv.gz is derived from the OpenFlights airlines database
(https://openflights.org/data.html, airlines.dat). The database is made available under the Open Database License
(ODbL) 1.0, https://opendatacommons.org/licenses/odbl/1-0/, and its individual contents under the Database Contents
License, https://opendatacommons.org/licenses/dbcl/1-0/. The derived file is shared here under the same ODbL.

Airports: waypoint/storage/airports.tsv.gz is derived from OurAirports' public-domain data
(https://ourairports.com/data/), through the airportsdata package (https://pypi.org/project/airportsdata/), which adds
time zones. waypoint/storage/regions.tsv.gz (each US airport's state, and country names) is derived from the same data.

Places: waypoint/storage/places.tsv.gz holds US ZIP code centres from the U.S. Census Bureau's 2023 Gazetteer ZIP Code
Tabulation Areas (US government data, public domain; https://www.census.gov/geographies/reference-files/time-series/geo/gazetteer-files.html)
and Canadian and British postal-code areas and the cities of 15,000 people or more from GeoNames
(https://www.geonames.org/, files GB.zip, CA.zip and cities15000.zip), which is licensed under Creative Commons
Attribution 4.0, https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/. The names and coordinates were rounded and combined; the
file is shared here under the same licence.

Interstates: waypoint/storage/roads.tsv.gz is derived from the National Highway System shapefile (version 2025-08-08,
nhs_2025-08-08.zip) published by the Federal Highway Administration, U.S. Department of Transportation
(https://www.fhwa.dot.gov/planning/national_highway_system/nhs_maps/), keeping the features signed and classed as
Interstate routes. This is US government data; its metadata states "Access Constraints: None" and that the NHS database,
or any portion of it, can be freely distributed as long as its metadata entry is included. The file combines the pieces
of each route into a network of junctions, simplifies their shapes to about 100 metres and rounds the coordinates; the
FHWA gives no warranty for it, and neither does Waypoint.

State lines: waypoint/storage/states.tsv.gz is derived from the 2024 Cartographic Boundary File for States and Equivalent
Entities for the United States at 1:5,000,000 (cb_2024_us_state_5m.zip) published by the U.S. Census Bureau, U.S. Department
of Commerce (https://www.census.gov/geographies/mapping-files/time-series/geo/cartographic-boundary.html). This is US
government data; its metadata states "Access constraints: None". The file keeps only the lines two states share, joins them
from one tripoint to the next, simplifies their shapes to about a kilometre and rounds the coordinates; the Census Bureau
gives no warranty for it, and neither does Waypoint.
